*> Implementation test of formats/src/zip.cob (ZIP-CRC-CHECK, ZIP-READ-RANGE, and the reasons of 22 §8.4):
*> ZIP-CRC-CHECK accepts a good entry (stored, deflated, a directory) and rejects the bad-CRC fixture
*> (FM-ZIP-CRC); ZIP-READ-RANGE inflates one entry into a caller buffer (stored, deflated, empty), reports
*> a buffer below the size (FM-ZIP-CAPACITY, the size in the length, the buffer untouched) and an
*> entry number out of range (FM-ZIP-NO-ENTRY); zip64 (an end record with a maximum field or a locator, and
*> an entry with the maximum sizes), several disks, encryption and a method other than 0 and 8 are rejected
*> with their own reason. Fixtures: contract/fixtures/formats (entries.zip, bad-crc.zip, encrypted.zip,
*> zip64.zip, basic.zip); end-record variants of entries.zip are made here under build/formats-test.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-ZIP-CRC-RANGE.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY FORMATS.
 01 WS-FIXTURE             PIC X(64).
 01 WS-PATH                PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-PATH-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ZIP                 USAGE POINTER.
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-INDEX               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(256).
 01 WS-NAME-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-AREA                PIC X(600).
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CRC                 BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED.
 01 WS-CRC-D               PIC 9(10).
 01 WS-ORIGINAL            PIC X(346).
 01 WS-WORK                PIC X(400).
 01 WS-WORK-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FFFF                PIC X(4).
 01 WS-ONE                 PIC X(2) VALUE X"0100".
 01 WS-LOCATOR             PIC X(20) VALUE LOW-VALUES.
 01 WS-SHOWN               PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-SHOWN2              PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-ACCESS              PIC X COMP-X VALUE 2.
 01 WS-DENY                PIC X COMP-X VALUE 0.
 01 WS-DEVICE              PIC X COMP-X VALUE 0.
 01 WS-HANDLE              PIC X(4).
 01 WS-OFFSET              PIC X(8) COMP-X.
 01 WS-BYTES               PIC X(4) COMP-X.
 01 WS-FLAGS               PIC X COMP-X VALUE 0.
 01 WS-DIRECTORY           PIC X(64).
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
*>   CRC check of good entries.
     MOVE "entries" TO WS-FIXTURE
     PERFORM OPEN-FIXTURE
     MOVE "stored.txt" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 10 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     PERFORM CHECK-NAMED
     MOVE "zip crc a stored entry matches its central CRC (status 0)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     MOVE "deflated.txt" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 12 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     PERFORM CHECK-NAMED
     MOVE "zip crc a deflated entry matches its central CRC (status 0)" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     MOVE "dir/" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 4 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     PERFORM CHECK-NAMED
     MOVE "zip crc a directory entry (no data, CRC 0) matches (status 0)" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-INDEX
     CALL "ZIP-CRC-CHECK" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip crc entry 0 is FM-ZIP-NO-ENTRY" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-ZIP-NO-ENTRY TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     MOVE 4 TO WS-INDEX
     CALL "ZIP-CRC-CHECK" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip crc entry 4 of 3 is FM-ZIP-NO-ENTRY" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS

*>   ZIP-READ-RANGE into a caller buffer.
     MOVE "deflated.txt" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 12 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
     MOVE 520 TO WS-CAPACITY
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-AREA
     CALL "ZIP-READ-RANGE" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-AREA WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-CRC
     CALL "CRC32" USING WS-AREA WS-LENGTH WS-CRC
     MOVE "zip range deflated.txt into a buffer of exactly 520 bytes: status 0, 520 bytes, central CRC 8004cf53"
         TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "0 520 2147798867" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-SHOWN
     MOVE WS-LENGTH TO WS-SHOWN2
     MOVE WS-CRC TO WS-CRC-D
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN2) " " WS-CRC-D DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 519 TO WS-CAPACITY
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-AREA
     CALL "ZIP-READ-RANGE" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-AREA WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip range a buffer of 519 bytes for 520: FM-ZIP-CAPACITY, length 520, buffer untouched" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "5 520 blank" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-SHOWN
     MOVE WS-LENGTH TO WS-SHOWN2
     IF WS-AREA = SPACES
         STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN2) " blank" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     ELSE
         STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN2) " written" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "stored.txt" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 10 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
     MOVE 600 TO WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "ZIP-READ-RANGE" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-AREA WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip range stored.txt: status 0, 13 bytes, the text" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0 13 stored entry" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-SHOWN
     MOVE WS-LENGTH TO WS-SHOWN2
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN2) " " WS-AREA(1:12) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "dir/" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 4 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
     MOVE 0 TO WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "ZIP-READ-RANGE" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-AREA WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip range of an empty entry into a buffer of 0 bytes: status 0, length 0" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-SHOWN
     MOVE WS-LENGTH TO WS-SHOWN2
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN2) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-INDEX
     CALL "ZIP-READ-RANGE" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-AREA WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip range entry 0 is FM-ZIP-NO-ENTRY, length 0" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "13 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-SHOWN
     MOVE WS-LENGTH TO WS-SHOWN2
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN2) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ZIP-CLOSE" USING WS-ZIP

*>   An entry with an empty deflate stream (2 bytes) inflates to nothing.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PATH
     MOVE "contract/fixtures/formats/basic.zip" TO WS-PATH
     MOVE 35 TO WS-PATH-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-OPEN" USING WS-PATH WS-PATH-LENGTH WS-ZIP WS-STATUS
     MOVE "empty.txt" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 9 TO WS-NAME-LENGTH
     PERFORM CHECK-NAMED
     MOVE "zip crc empty.txt (deflated, 2 bytes, size 0) matches (status 0)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     CALL "ZIP-READ-RANGE" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-AREA WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip range empty.txt: status 0, length 0" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     CALL "ZIP-CLOSE" USING WS-ZIP

*>   The bad-CRC fixture.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PATH
     MOVE "contract/fixtures/formats/zip/bad-crc.zip" TO WS-PATH
     MOVE 41 TO WS-PATH-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-OPEN" USING WS-PATH WS-PATH-LENGTH WS-ZIP WS-STATUS
     MOVE 1 TO WS-INDEX
     CALL "ZIP-CRC-CHECK" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip crc bad-crc.zip: FM-ZIP-CRC" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-ZIP-CRC TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     MOVE 100 TO WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "ZIP-READ-RANGE" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-AREA WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip range bad-crc.zip still reads the data (status 0, 25 bytes): the CRC is ZIP-CRC-CHECK's" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0 25" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-SHOWN
     MOVE WS-LENGTH TO WS-SHOWN2
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN2) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ZIP-CLOSE" USING WS-ZIP
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE

*>   Encryption and zip64 entries: their own reasons, from both calls; ZIP-READ keeps status 2.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PATH
     MOVE "contract/fixtures/formats/zip/encrypted.zip" TO WS-PATH
     MOVE 43 TO WS-PATH-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-OPEN" USING WS-PATH WS-PATH-LENGTH WS-ZIP WS-STATUS
     MOVE 1 TO WS-INDEX
     MOVE 100 TO WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "ZIP-READ-RANGE" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-AREA WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip range encrypted.zip: FM-ZIP-ENCRYPTED" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-ZIP-ENCRYPTED TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     CALL "ZIP-CRC-CHECK" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip crc encrypted.zip: FM-ZIP-ENCRYPTED" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     CALL "ZIP-READ" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-AREA WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip read encrypted.zip keeps status 2 (corrupt or unsupported)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     CALL "ZIP-CLOSE" USING WS-ZIP
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PATH
     MOVE "contract/fixtures/formats/zip/zip64.zip" TO WS-PATH
     MOVE 39 TO WS-PATH-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-OPEN" USING WS-PATH WS-PATH-LENGTH WS-ZIP WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip zip64.zip opens (the entry carries the marker, the end record is plain)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     MOVE 1 TO WS-INDEX
     CALL "ZIP-READ-RANGE" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-AREA WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip range zip64.zip entry: FM-ZIP-ZIP64" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-ZIP-ZIP64 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     CALL "ZIP-CRC-CHECK" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip crc zip64.zip entry: FM-ZIP-ZIP64" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     CALL "ZIP-READ" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-AREA WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip read zip64.zip entry keeps status 2" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     CALL "ZIP-CLOSE" USING WS-ZIP

*>   End record variants of entries.zip (the end record starts at byte 324).
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PATH
     MOVE "contract/fixtures/formats/zip/entries.zip" TO WS-PATH
     MOVE 41 TO WS-PATH-LENGTH
     MOVE 346 TO WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "FILE-READ-ALL" USING WS-PATH WS-PATH-LENGTH WS-ORIGINAL WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip the entries.zip fixture is 346 bytes" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 346 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-LENGTH TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF WS-STATUS NOT = 0
         MOVE -1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE ALL X"FF" TO WS-FFFF

     MOVE WS-ORIGINAL TO WS-WORK
     MOVE 346 TO WS-WORK-LENGTH
     PERFORM OPEN-WORK
     MOVE "zip the unpatched copy of entries.zip opens (status 0)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     CALL "ZIP-CLOSE" USING WS-ZIP

     MOVE WS-ORIGINAL TO WS-WORK
     MOVE WS-FFFF(1:2) TO WS-WORK(333:2)
     MOVE WS-FFFF(1:2) TO WS-WORK(335:2)
     PERFORM OPEN-WORK
     MOVE "zip an end record with 65535 entries is FM-ZIP-ZIP64" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-ZIP-ZIP64 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS

     MOVE WS-ORIGINAL TO WS-WORK
     MOVE WS-FFFF TO WS-WORK(337:4)
     PERFORM OPEN-WORK
     MOVE "zip an end record with a central directory size of ffffffff is FM-ZIP-ZIP64" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS

     MOVE WS-ORIGINAL TO WS-WORK
     MOVE WS-FFFF TO WS-WORK(341:4)
     PERFORM OPEN-WORK
     MOVE "zip an end record with a central directory offset of ffffffff is FM-ZIP-ZIP64" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS

     MOVE WS-ORIGINAL(1:324) TO WS-WORK(1:324)
     MOVE "PK" TO WS-LOCATOR(1:2)
     MOVE X"0607" TO WS-LOCATOR(3:2)
     MOVE WS-LOCATOR TO WS-WORK(325:20)
     MOVE WS-ORIGINAL(325:22) TO WS-WORK(345:22)
     MOVE 366 TO WS-WORK-LENGTH
     PERFORM OPEN-WORK
     MOVE "zip an end record after a zip64 end record locator is FM-ZIP-ZIP64" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS

     MOVE WS-ORIGINAL TO WS-WORK
     MOVE 346 TO WS-WORK-LENGTH
     MOVE WS-ONE TO WS-WORK(329:2)
     PERFORM OPEN-WORK
     MOVE "zip an end record of disk 1 is FM-ZIP-MULTI-DISK" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-ZIP-MULTI-DISK TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS

     MOVE WS-ORIGINAL TO WS-WORK
     MOVE WS-ONE TO WS-WORK(331:2)
     PERFORM OPEN-WORK
     MOVE "zip an end record whose central directory starts on disk 1 is FM-ZIP-MULTI-DISK" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS

     MOVE WS-ORIGINAL TO WS-WORK
     MOVE WS-ONE TO WS-WORK(333:2)
     PERFORM OPEN-WORK
     MOVE "zip an end record whose two entry counts differ stays FM-ZIP-CORRUPT" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-ZIP-CORRUPT TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS

*>   A method other than 0 and 8 (method 12 in the central record of stored.txt, at byte 170).
     MOVE WS-ORIGINAL TO WS-WORK
     MOVE X"0C00" TO WS-WORK(171:2)
     PERFORM OPEN-WORK
     MOVE "zip the patched entries.zip opens (status 0)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     MOVE 1 TO WS-INDEX
     MOVE 100 TO WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "ZIP-READ-RANGE" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-AREA WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip range an entry of method 12 is FM-ZIP-METHOD" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-ZIP-METHOD TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     CALL "ZIP-CRC-CHECK" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip crc an entry of method 12 is FM-ZIP-METHOD" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     CALL "ZIP-READ" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-AREA WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip read an entry of method 12 keeps status 2" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     CALL "ZIP-CLOSE" USING WS-ZIP

*>   A damaged archive: the end record of a file that is not a zip stays status 2.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PATH
     MOVE "contract/fixtures/formats/zip/not-a-zip.bin" TO WS-PATH
     MOVE 43 TO WS-PATH-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-OPEN" USING WS-PATH WS-PATH-LENGTH WS-ZIP WS-STATUS
     MOVE "zip not-a-zip.bin is FM-ZIP-CORRUPT" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-ZIP-CORRUPT TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-STATUS
     STOP RUN.

 OPEN-FIXTURE.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PATH
     STRING "contract/fixtures/formats/zip/" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-FIXTURE) ".zip" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-PATH
     COMPUTE WS-PATH-LENGTH = 34 + FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-FIXTURE))
     CALL "ZIP-OPEN" USING WS-PATH WS-PATH-LENGTH WS-ZIP WS-STATUS
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE.

 CHECK-NAMED.
     CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-INDEX
     CALL "ZIP-CRC-CHECK" USING WS-ZIP WS-INDEX WS-STATUS.

 ASSERT-STATUS.
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

*> Writes WS-WORK (WS-WORK-LENGTH bytes) to build/formats-test/variant.zip and opens it.
 OPEN-WORK.
     MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-DIRECTORY
     MOVE "build/formats-test" TO WS-DIRECTORY
     CALL "CBL_CREATE_DIR" USING WS-DIRECTORY
     MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-PATH
     MOVE "build/formats-test/variant.zip" TO WS-PATH
     CALL "CBL_CREATE_FILE" USING WS-PATH WS-ACCESS WS-DENY WS-DEVICE WS-HANDLE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-OFFSET
     MOVE WS-WORK-LENGTH TO WS-BYTES
     CALL "CBL_WRITE_FILE" USING WS-HANDLE WS-OFFSET WS-BYTES WS-FLAGS WS-WORK
     CALL "CBL_CLOSE_FILE" USING WS-HANDLE
     MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
     MOVE 30 TO WS-PATH-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-OPEN" USING WS-PATH WS-PATH-LENGTH WS-ZIP WS-STATUS
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE.
 END PROGRAM TEST-ZIP-CRC-RANGE.
